Paragraph 2 delves into diversity-based query result diversification as a related line of study in information retrieval and explains how it differs from existing approaches by focusing on providing diverse outputs that cover different aspects or interpretations of the query. It also highlights the relevance of this approach to the proposed problem IDT, which considers both quality (relevance) and diversity when returning tuples to users.

